            <div xml:id="d485">

                <pb facs="0609" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg507"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 13329/4–5.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Ambassador O’Brien.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-06-05"><hi rendition="#italic">June 5,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The department approves your note of May 2,
                    1908, to the Japanese minister for foreign affairs upon the occasion of the
                    explosion on board the Japanese ship of war <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Matsushima</hi>, copy of which you inclose with your dispatch No. 309, of
                    the same date.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
